$DIR/main.p:19:11: q holds a view of v (v.Slice(), line 15), which was given a new value at line 18, so q can no longer be used here
    q looks at memory that v owns, without owning it: the view was made by
    v.Slice() at line 15. A view of an owner held in a local variable may be
    used only while the variable keeps the value the view was made from. At line
    18 v was given a new value, so the view may look at memory that was
    released, or at a value that now belongs to something else.
    Go keeps memory alive for as long as any pointer refers to it. Plutonium has
    no garbage collector: an owner releases its memory when it is dropped, so a
    view must not be used after the value it looks at has gone.
    Use q before line 18, or give v its new value only after the last use of q
    Or make the view again after line 18:
        q = v.Slice()
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3313" for a longer explanation)
